# Temperature-driven within-host pathogen dynamics in vector-borne plant epidemics
===

## Overview

This repository contains the code and processed data used in the study of temperature-driven within-host pathogen dynamics in vector-borne plant epidemics.

The goal of this project is to analyze how environmental temperature influences pathogen development and transmission dynamics in plant disease systems.

---

## Repository structure

- `Results.ipynb` – main notebook with simulations, analysis, and figures  
- `vector_borne_functions.py` – core model functions used in the simulations  
- `real_data/` – processed datasets used in the analysis (raw NetCDF files are excluded due to size limitations)  
- `figures/` – figures generated for the manuscript  

---

## Data

Due to size limitations imposed by GitHub, raw NetCDF (`.nc`) climate datasets are not included in this repository.

Only processed datasets required to reproduce the results are provided.

If needed, raw data can be obtained from external sources (e.g. CHELSA climate database).

---

